import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How to use this site — The Gentle AI Guide"
  description="Three simple things to know about reading The Gentle AI Guide: where to start, how to move between guides, and how to make the text bigger."
>
  <section class="page-top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>How to use this site</h1>
      <p class="lede">Three things to know. That's all.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>1. Start with guide 1</h2>
      <p>The five guides are numbered. Guide 1 explains what AI actually is. The others build on it. If you only read one, read that one.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/guides/what-is-ai/">Go to guide 1</a></p>

      <h2>2. Use the buttons at the bottom of each guide</h2>
      <p>When you reach the end of a guide, you'll see two large boxes: <strong>Previous</strong> and <strong>Next</strong>. They tell you exactly which guide they lead to. You never have to remember where you were — the top of every guide says "Guide 2 of 5", and the bar under it shows how far you've come.</p>

      <h2>3. Make the text bigger if you like</h2>
      <p>At the top of every page, next to the site name, there are three buttons: <strong>A</strong>, <strong>A+</strong> and <strong>A++</strong>. Press A+ or A++ and everything on the site gets bigger. The site remembers your choice next time you visit.</p>

      <h2>If something is unclear</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@gentleaiguide.com">hello@gentleaiguide.com</a>. Questions from readers often become new guides.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
